: "Level at move 20, then one stone on F4", "summary": "The 14k won as White by 8 points. Opus 5.5 fought its way back to an even game, 0.0 at move 20, then F4 on turn 21 lost 10.2 points and put it at -10.2. The rest of the game was quiet endgame, with the lead staying near -7.9 until the final two passes.", "moments": [{"turn": 9, "text": "Opus 5.5 extended with E4 and the lead went from -1.1 to -6.4, a loss of 5.2 points. The engine preferred F4. The stones on D4, E4 and E5 faced a White row on D3 and E3."}, {"turn": 10, "text": "The 14k answered with F3, which lost 5.2 points of its own and moved the lead from -6.4 back to -1.2. The engine wanted F4 there too, so the gap Opus 5.5 left was handed straight back."}, {"turn": 16, "text": "White's G8 lost 3.4 points (-3.3 to +0.1) and the engine would have played C2. That left Black level and slightly ahead, with a wall of Black stones on F6, F7 and E8 against White's G-file stones."}, {"turn": 21, "text": "The decisive move. With the game level at -0.0, Opus 5.5 played F4 between E4 and G4, and the lead fell to -10.2, a loss of 10.2 points. The engine's choice was D2, on the second line below White's row-3 wall. White's C2 on the next turn changed the lead by only 0.0."}, {"turn": 26, "text": "After Opus 5.5's A3 lost 2.2 points (-10.3 to -12.5), the lead was at its worst. White's A2 then lost 4.6 points of its own, with the engine preferring E7, and the lead came back to -7.9. The corner finished with White on A2, B2 and C2 beneath Black's row-3 stones, and the margin never moved much after that."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "libs.py flood-fills each group on a pasted board and prints its stones and liberties, and count.py flood-fills empty regions to tally territory with dead stones removed; both only analyze the position given and never generate, score, or rank candidate moves or look ahead.", "stop": false}}